            'Uses and forecasts grade specific enrollment and dropout rates for primary and lower secondary
            'Other New_Init routines - IfsEducPri, PrimaryTotals, ProcessPriNet, OverAgeCalcNew, EducSaveForNextYear

            '----------- Education Module Main ---------------
            '
            '   Module developed by collaboration of Mohammod T. Irfan and Barry B. Hughes
            '   Model code available for review and education only
            '   Reproduction or incorporation in other software by permission only
            '   Last changed by BBH or MTI: 2007
            '
            '
            '   AGE COHORTS:  0=INFANTS (for transition calculation); 1=0-4 YEARS;
            '                    2 = 5-9 (primary); 3=10-14 (lower secondary);4=15-19; 5=20-24 YEARS;
            '                    6 = 25-29;... 17=80-84; 18=85-89; 19=90-94; 20=95-99; 21=100+
            '
            '  We are using one year cohorts for flows; 5 year cohorts for stocks

            '   Net Intake Rate is the entrance-age new entrants expressed as a percentage of entering-age population, the rate cannot go over 100%
            '   Gross Intake Rate is the entrants, of any age, as a percentage of entering-age children population, could be higher than 100%
            '   Survival Rate is the percentage of all entrants who reach the final grade,  the rate cannot go over 100%

            '   Net Enrolment rate is the number of school-age students expressed as a percentage of the population of school-age, the rate cannot go over 100%
            '   Net enrollment can include students who are over/under-age for the grade, but still of-age for the schooling level

            '   Gross Enrolment rate is total students, irrespective of age, expressed as a percentage of the population of the children at school-age, the rate can go over 100%
            '   Graduation (or completion) rate is the number of graduates expressed as a percentage of graduating age children, these are gross rates and can go above 100%
            '   Transition rate is the number of final graders of a certain level who enroll in the first grade of the next levelin the subsequent year, it is expreassed as a percentage rate that cannot exceed 100

            '   Grade enrollment rates are gross enrollment rates for a single-year grade, all students in the grade expressed as a percentage of the population of the officila age for the grade
            '   Grade dropout rates are num ber of students who drop out of a grade expressed as a percentage of total enrollment for the grade

            '   Gross rates could have pupils of any age at the numerator, net rates would have pupils of appropriate age only
            '   Thus, while gross rates can go beyond 100, nets can not
            '   This line of code saved for debugging--  If GRPS(1,R%) = "Chad" Then Stop


